  "challenge": "The line economics are internally coherent as a net credit, not garbage: −5 × $250 (WidgetA) + 2 × $500 (WidgetB) = −$250, which exactly matches the stated total—so AR-002/AR-004 are largely an artifact of a mis-stated subtotal rather than an unintelligible document. Both items exist, are active, and match catalog reference prices exactly ($250 and $500). INV-1009 has no prior submission, so this is not a replay. Negative quantity and negative total are the normal shape of a return-plus-offset purchase; the innocent reading is a credit memo / RMA mis-labeled as an invoice (policy text for AR-005/AR-006 even frames the remedy as “credit memo”), with the empty vendor possibly a JSON extraction gap rather than a true no-payee. Flat REJECT discards a plausible legitimate credit that should be re-typed or routed as a credit memo once the payee is supplied, not treated as an unpayable nullity.",
